; Fish base as TWO sequential rabbit ears: triangle abd flattened at its
; incenter, then triangle cbd at its own — two independent single-vertex
; statements on opposite sides of the b-d line. The second flatten's rays
; never touch the first ear's folded material (it all lies strictly on the
; other side, and both incenters' emergent rays stay on their own sides),
; so the all-layers guard must judge the actual crease SEGMENTS — judging
; each ray's infinite line instead hits the first ear's far-away flaps and
; rejects a physically sound fold ("collapse through unaligned layers").

paper square

mark --diag = map .a onto .c
mark --ray = through .a .c

step left
mark --l1 = map --ab onto --diag
mark --l2 = map --da onto --diag
flatten (--l1 & .b) (--l2 & .d) (--ray & .a) {toward .d}

step right
mark --l3 = map --cd onto --diag
mark --l4 = map --bc onto --diag
flatten (--l3 & .d) (--l4 & .b) (--ray & .c) {toward .d}

; assert steps = 4
; assert faces = 12
